Two Pointers Algorithms: resource "AlgomasterIO youtube"

What problems could use this? == Linear Data Structures 
- arrays (sorted or palindrome)
- strings 
- linked list
- both used to reduce time complexity O(n^2) --> O(n)

3 most common strats
- Converging pointers: opposite directions and move into a converging point. 
    ex. Palindrome
    "abcdcba"  --> "abcdcba"
     *     *          **

- Parallel pointers: both start at same point, both move right. R pointer is exploratory, while L pointer is track progress
    ex. Sliding window technique
    3, 1, -2, 6, 7, 5   -->  3, 1, -2, 6, 7, 5
    L     R                         L  R 

- Trigger-Based Pointers: R pointer moves right until condition is met, then start L pointer to find additional info. 
    ex. Finding Nth node in a linked list.
    1->3->5->7->9->11   e.g. condition is "7"  --> move both pointers at same interval until it reaches the end.
    L        R

When to use?
- Linear data structures
- Return a pair of values under a condition

